WEBVTT

00:00:12.450 --> 00:00:18.600
Do you hear?  Hooves beating

00:00:25.430 --> 00:00:30.750
A carriage goes through the gentle hills

00:00:33.050 --> 00:00:37.980
Someone comes to pick me up

00:00:39.070 --> 00:00:45.950
And takes me

00:00:46.200 --> 00:00:49.900
To the avenue with white flowers

00:00:52.620 --> 00:00:58.050
To the home of wind

00:00:58.950 --> 00:01:02.400
He takes me

00:01:05.200 --> 00:01:08.900
I'm sure

00:01:38.500 --> 00:01:42.110
...The girl was taken to the sea.

00:01:42.560 --> 00:01:46.360
Then she was laid in a black samite.

00:01:46.990 --> 00:01:50.240
Her two brethren kissed her quiet brows

00:01:50.240 --> 00:01:52.960
and parted all in tears saying to her:

00:01:53.230 --> 00:01:56.170
'Sister, farewell for ever.'

00:01:56.580 --> 00:01:58.750
'Farewell, sweet sister.'

00:02:06.630 --> 00:02:10.990
All her bright hair was streaming down
the cloth of gold.

00:02:10.990 --> 00:02:13.520
In her right hand the lily,

00:02:13.930 --> 00:02:17.090
in her left the letter.

00:02:19.840 --> 00:02:22.360
Her clear-featured face was lovely,

00:02:22.450 --> 00:02:26.490
for she did not seem as dead,

00:02:26.930 --> 00:02:32.700
but fast asleep, and lay as though she smiled,

00:02:33.560 --> 00:02:40.120
as she headed to the castle of Camelot
where the knight of her dreams lived.

00:02:41.580 --> 00:02:45.240
Most noble lord, Sir Lancelot du Lac,

00:02:45.960 --> 00:02:51.160
you left me taking no farewell,
so I come to take my last farewell of you.

00:02:51.790 --> 00:02:58.570
I loved you, and my love had no return,

00:02:59.920 --> 00:03:06.690
and therefore my true love has been my death.

00:03:07.740 --> 00:03:10.270
Oh! Sir Lancelot!

00:03:10.270 --> 00:03:11.590
Anne! Anne!

00:03:11.590 --> 00:03:14.300
What are you doing? The fish is on the hook!

00:03:17.920 --> 00:03:18.890
It's true!

00:03:19.350 --> 00:03:21.380
How strong! Everyone help me out!
Hurry, hurry!

00:03:21.380 --> 00:03:22.300
Really?

00:03:22.300 --> 00:03:24.040
Calm down, Anne! Don't let it go!

00:03:24.360 --> 00:03:26.420
Summer, August,

00:03:26.920 --> 00:03:29.510
Anne's hair had regained her former glory.

00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:32.020
Anne, Diana,

00:03:32.280 --> 00:03:34.690
Jane and Ruby,

00:03:34.900 --> 00:03:40.170
members of the Story Club, came
everyday to the Lake of Shining Waters

00:03:40.600 --> 00:03:45.480
to enjoy themselves during their free time.

00:03:51.050 --> 00:03:52.980
What a pity, the fish was large too.

00:03:52.980 --> 00:03:54.980
It was in the hook for some time...

00:03:55.230 --> 00:03:56.570
Didn't you notice?

00:03:56.630 --> 00:03:57.340
No...

00:03:57.430 --> 00:03:58.550
Because I...

00:03:59.160 --> 00:04:00.680
Were you day-dreaming again, Anne?

00:04:01.680 --> 00:04:03.820
I was in the Camelot castle!

00:04:04.430 --> 00:04:05.670
Camelot?

00:04:05.730 --> 00:04:09.170
Are you talking about King Arthur and
the Knights of the Round Table?

00:04:09.290 --> 00:04:11.160
And That is in Camelot.

00:04:11.550 --> 00:04:14.450
Oh, if we were born in Camelot,

00:04:15.120 --> 00:04:18.310
our lives wouldn't be so mundane.

00:04:18.310 --> 00:04:21.350
It would be more exciting and romantic.

00:04:22.650 --> 00:04:24.100
That could be possible.

00:04:24.290 --> 00:04:26.800
Great knight, Sir Lancelot!

00:04:26.950 --> 00:04:29.660
I respect you with all my heart.

00:04:30.610 --> 00:04:32.360
But it's truly wonderful.

00:04:32.360 --> 00:04:36.790
I'm so glad to learn about the story
of Sir Lancelot and the Lily Maid, Elaine.

00:04:36.880 --> 00:04:37.790
That's right.

00:04:38.070 --> 00:04:39.820
The Lily Maid died for love,

00:04:39.820 --> 00:04:44.600
and her body was sent to Camelot
where Sir Lancelot dwelled.

00:04:44.600 --> 00:04:47.040
It was really exciting.

00:04:47.400 --> 00:04:54.630
But I wouldn't never be able to die
for a man after being rejected by him.

00:04:54.690 --> 00:04:56.230
I'm not that romantic.

00:04:56.230 --> 00:04:57.820
Oh, Ruby!

00:04:58.940 --> 00:05:01.440
But Elaine chose the wrong man to love.

00:05:01.440 --> 00:05:04.840
Sir Lancelot had already given
his heart to Guinevere

00:05:04.840 --> 00:05:07.580
and promised to never marry anyone else.

00:05:07.650 --> 00:05:10.470
But I feel really sorry for Elaine.

00:05:10.470 --> 00:05:13.470
When Lancelot asked for her wish,
she said:

00:05:13.660 --> 00:05:18.900
'I have gone mad. I love you: let me die'.
It was just like this, wasn't it?

00:05:19.070 --> 00:05:23.890
When I think about her feelings at
that time, tears come to my eyes.

00:05:24.010 --> 00:05:24.920
I feel the same.

00:05:24.920 --> 00:05:26.270
Me too.

00:05:26.520 --> 00:05:28.520
Oh, Sir Lancelot,

00:05:29.300 --> 00:05:34.160
not to be with you, not to see your face...

00:05:35.180 --> 00:05:38.170
Alas for me then, my good days are done.

00:05:40.200 --> 00:05:46.500
O sweet father, tender and true, deny me not.
Ye never yet denied my fancies.

00:05:46.780 --> 00:05:51.390
Lay the letter in my hand
a little ere I die, and close the hand Upon it.

00:05:51.550 --> 00:05:55.260
Father, take me to the river,
and a barge be ready on the river...

00:05:59.580 --> 00:06:01.180
A barge be ready on the river...

00:06:05.770 --> 00:06:07.010
What's wrong, Anne?

00:06:07.320 --> 00:06:09.470
Of course,

00:06:09.470 --> 00:06:11.390
this is worth trying.

00:06:12.400 --> 00:06:15.110
Everyone, I have a great idea.

00:06:16.020 --> 00:06:19.410
Let's all act out the story of the Lily Maid.

00:06:19.410 --> 00:06:21.170
Right here, right now.

00:06:21.290 --> 00:06:22.070
What?

00:06:22.070 --> 00:06:23.630
The stage is already set.

00:06:23.880 --> 00:06:26.140
The barge of the deceased Lily Maid...

00:06:26.450 --> 00:06:28.240
Look, it's right there.

00:06:28.500 --> 00:06:33.640
All we need is a person on the
flat to play the deceased Lily Maid.

00:06:33.640 --> 00:06:34.810
Oh, good idea.

00:06:34.990 --> 00:06:40.810
And the others can be her siblings,

00:06:40.810 --> 00:06:43.620
pushing that flat to the river.

00:06:43.960 --> 00:06:44.780
What?

00:06:44.780 --> 00:06:46.140
Don't worry.

00:06:46.800 --> 00:06:49.560
The flat will drift down
with the current under the bridge

00:06:49.560 --> 00:06:53.960
and strand itself in the land
at the curve of the pond.

00:06:54.230 --> 00:06:57.020
I get it.
That would be Camelot!

00:06:57.200 --> 00:06:58.290
That's right!

00:06:58.620 --> 00:07:03.140
When the flat starts drifting down,
the other 3 will run to the headland.

00:07:03.220 --> 00:07:05.580
And pretend to be King Arthur and Guinevere.

00:07:05.580 --> 00:07:08.670
And Lancelot who waits for her.

00:07:08.800 --> 00:07:11.640
Well? Don't you think it's a good idea?

00:07:13.150 --> 00:07:14.860
Then let's try it!

00:07:16.300 --> 00:07:17.800
Fantastic, Anne!

00:07:18.140 --> 00:07:19.450
Let's do it!

00:07:19.450 --> 00:07:22.060
It will be good for our Story club!

00:07:22.060 --> 00:07:24.690
You're right! Let's do it!

00:07:33.150 --> 00:07:34.470
Well, Ruby?

00:07:35.230 --> 00:07:36.450
N-no, no, no!

00:07:36.680 --> 00:07:38.580
Even if someone is waiting there I won't go!

00:07:38.580 --> 00:07:42.400
To lie down and pretend
I was dead... I just couldn't.

00:07:42.700 --> 00:07:44.400
I'd die really of fright.

00:07:46.490 --> 00:07:47.330
Not me!

00:07:47.330 --> 00:07:50.810
I'd be popping up every
minute or so to see where I was!

00:07:54.240 --> 00:07:56.890
Diana, it's a good thing
that you brought this shawl.

00:07:57.570 --> 00:08:00.610
This black shawl is good to
pall the barge in black samite.

00:08:01.240 --> 00:08:03.270
There. With this, everything is ready.

00:08:05.090 --> 00:08:06.330
What's wrong?

00:08:06.580 --> 00:08:10.290
Well, we were thinking
that you should play Elaine, Anne.

00:08:10.290 --> 00:08:13.370
T-that's right.
It was you who thought of it.

00:08:13.610 --> 00:08:16.580
Of course I would like to play Elaine,
but I am not suitable.

00:08:16.590 --> 00:08:20.870
So let's think through who
would be the best Lily Maid.

00:08:21.630 --> 00:08:26.770
Ruby, you ought to be Elaine because you are
so fair and have such lovely long bright hair.

00:08:27.250 --> 00:08:30.700
Elaine had 'all her bright hair streaming
down,' you know.

00:08:31.130 --> 00:08:33.000
So you should be the Lily Maid.

00:08:33.000 --> 00:08:37.260
N-no, I won't do it. I already rejected
that role earlier, so now I can't do it.

00:08:37.530 --> 00:08:44.300
Anne, your complexion is just as fair as Ruby's.
And your hair is as long as before. And...

00:08:44.300 --> 00:08:48.230
But it's so ridiculous to
have a redheaded Elaine.

00:08:49.260 --> 00:08:51.960
That's not true! It's all right!

00:08:54.460 --> 00:08:58.690
To tell the truth, none of us have
the courage to go alone on the boat.

00:09:05.370 --> 00:09:06.200
All right.

00:09:06.420 --> 00:09:08.730
I'll be Lily Maid.

00:09:15.320 --> 00:09:19.720
But I really think it's weird to
have a redheaded Elaine.

00:09:19.720 --> 00:09:21.310
It's all right!

00:09:21.310 --> 00:09:23.930
You won't be able to see it
with your eyes closed...

00:09:27.210 --> 00:09:30.630
Then Ruby, you must be King Arthur
and Jane will be Guinevere

00:09:30.630 --> 00:09:32.420
and Diana must be Lancelot.

00:09:33.330 --> 00:09:36.450
But first you must be Elaine's brothers.

00:09:39.700 --> 00:09:41.090
We need flowers!

00:09:41.090 --> 00:09:43.030
Diana, where is your shawl?

00:09:43.030 --> 00:09:44.030
It's over there!

00:09:47.830 --> 00:09:50.390
Oh! It's looks just like her!

00:09:50.640 --> 00:09:53.540
But she looks more
like Iris Maid than Lily Maid.

00:09:54.550 --> 00:09:57.630
And this also doesn't
look much like Cloth of gold.

00:10:14.000 --> 00:10:16.300
She does look really dead.

00:10:16.390 --> 00:10:17.340
That's true.

00:10:19.500 --> 00:10:21.200
Don't open your eyes.

00:10:21.490 --> 00:10:22.810
You're supposed to be dead.

00:10:23.000 --> 00:10:25.680
Please don't utter nonsense.

00:10:26.220 --> 00:10:26.510
Sorry.

00:10:26.510 --> 00:10:27.370
I'm sorry.

00:10:27.850 --> 00:10:29.150
Then let's begin.

00:10:30.070 --> 00:10:32.150
Your faces have to look sadder.

00:10:35.300 --> 00:10:37.590
Oh, my sweet sister...

00:10:38.950 --> 00:10:42.410
Anne, for goodness sake smile a little.

00:10:43.300 --> 00:10:46.320
You know Elaine
'lay as though she smiled.'

00:10:48.670 --> 00:10:49.940
That's better.

00:10:51.190 --> 00:10:53.370
Oh, my sweet sister...

00:10:53.530 --> 00:10:55.010
Farewell...

00:11:04.200 --> 00:11:06.650
Farewell, sweet sister...

00:11:09.840 --> 00:11:12.550
Sister, farewell forever.

00:11:25.290 --> 00:11:26.360
What's wrong?

00:11:26.580 --> 00:11:27.740
Push harder.

00:11:27.900 --> 00:11:28.900
How strange.

00:11:29.800 --> 00:11:30.410
Now!

00:11:53.180 --> 00:11:55.180
It's all right. It's floating towards the bridge.

00:11:55.180 --> 00:11:56.280
Yes.

00:11:56.970 --> 00:11:58.840
Then let's rush to Camelot!

00:11:58.840 --> 00:11:59.560
Yes!

00:12:07.870 --> 00:12:08.970
Run faster, Ruby!

00:12:09.020 --> 00:12:09.970
I'm running!

00:12:18.350 --> 00:12:22.740
All her bright hair was streaming down
the cloth of gold.

00:12:23.090 --> 00:12:25.810
In her right hand the lily,

00:12:25.810 --> 00:12:28.750
in her left the letter.

00:12:30.140 --> 00:12:32.520
Her clear-featured face was lovely,

00:12:32.520 --> 00:12:36.790
for she did not seem as dead,

00:12:37.140 --> 00:12:42.410
but fast asleep, and lay as though she smiled,

00:12:42.800 --> 00:12:49.780
as she headed to the castle of Camelot
where the knight of her dreams lived.

00:13:27.950 --> 00:13:30.960
There's a hole on the boat!
What will I do?

00:13:48.860 --> 00:13:50.110
Is there anybody?

00:13:58.080 --> 00:14:03.860
Dear God, please take the flat
close to a pile and I'll do the rest!

00:14:03.860 --> 00:14:06.050
Please don't let it pass by the middle!

00:14:07.090 --> 00:14:09.910
Oh god! I have one more wish!

00:14:09.910 --> 00:14:14.040
Don't let the flat sink
before arriving to the bridge!

00:14:14.040 --> 00:14:17.260
I promise that I'll always be good after that!

00:14:33.650 --> 00:14:35.110
Oh! God!

00:15:11.900 --> 00:15:14.860
Jane! Ruby! She's coming!
Anne is coming!

00:15:16.730 --> 00:15:18.340
You're right! She's coming!

00:15:20.930 --> 00:15:22.780
Stop! You shouldn't clap!

00:15:22.780 --> 00:15:23.780
You're right!

00:15:25.250 --> 00:15:26.180
Be quiet!

00:15:27.250 --> 00:15:30.720
Arthur and the others
shouldn't have seen the boat yet.

00:15:30.720 --> 00:15:31.440
You're right.

00:15:39.800 --> 00:15:41.440
Look! Look!

00:15:48.490 --> 00:15:49.720
The boat sank.

00:15:51.590 --> 00:15:53.480
Hey, the boat sank.

00:15:56.470 --> 00:15:58.210
Anne!

00:15:58.220 --> 00:15:59.550
Anne Shirley!

00:16:00.840 --> 00:16:02.090
Where are you?

00:16:02.210 --> 00:16:03.440
Answer me!

00:16:06.480 --> 00:16:08.810
I'll go home to tell my mother!

00:16:08.810 --> 00:16:10.640
Wait, Diana! I'm coming too!

00:16:10.770 --> 00:16:11.640
Me too!

00:16:34.140 --> 00:16:35.060
Diana!

00:16:35.140 --> 00:16:36.700
Jane! Ruby!

00:16:38.820 --> 00:16:40.080
Diana, wait!

00:16:40.230 --> 00:16:43.650
It's me! I'm here! Help me!

00:16:46.090 --> 00:16:48.670
Jane! Ruby! Diana!

00:17:13.490 --> 00:17:15.800
Someone! There's someone over there!

00:17:20.040 --> 00:17:22.310
Hey! Hey!!

00:17:22.310 --> 00:17:26.200
Help me!
You fishing on the boat!

00:17:27.440 --> 00:17:31.380
Over here! Here!
Under the bridge!

00:17:33.860 --> 00:17:34.710
Gil...

00:17:34.970 --> 00:17:36.090
Anne...!

00:17:36.590 --> 00:17:39.670
Anne Shirley! How on earth did you get there?

00:17:44.100 --> 00:17:45.070
Be careful!

00:17:54.130 --> 00:17:56.000
Anne, come on up!

00:17:58.980 --> 00:18:01.360
What are you waiting for?
Grab my hand!

00:18:03.570 --> 00:18:04.570
Be careful!

00:18:07.130 --> 00:18:10.070
I'm sorry. You saved me.

00:18:10.650 --> 00:18:11.810
Thank you.

00:18:11.880 --> 00:18:14.960
Don't worry. But you're soaked!

00:18:15.200 --> 00:18:16.160
Are you hurt?

00:18:16.410 --> 00:18:17.940
No, I'm fine.

00:18:18.810 --> 00:18:22.340
Will you be kind enough to
row me to the landing?

00:18:22.740 --> 00:18:26.500
You're right. I'll take you right away.
You could catch a cold.

00:18:32.150 --> 00:18:35.130
I was shocked to see you there.

00:18:35.680 --> 00:18:37.490
What has happened?

00:18:38.300 --> 00:18:41.570
We were playing Elaine.

00:18:44.310 --> 00:18:45.820
I don't remember this part in that story.

00:19:05.270 --> 00:19:06.450
I'm very much obliged to you.

00:19:07.020 --> 00:19:08.440
Anne, please wait.

00:19:09.390 --> 00:19:11.570
Can't we be good friends?

00:19:11.920 --> 00:19:15.640
I'm awfully sorry I
made fun of your hair that time.

00:19:16.290 --> 00:19:19.710
I didn't mean to vex
you and I only meant it for a joke.

00:19:20.320 --> 00:19:22.650
Besides, it's so long ago.

00:19:23.190 --> 00:19:25.810
I think
your hair is awfully pretty now.

00:19:26.020 --> 00:19:27.030
Honest I do.

00:19:32.700 --> 00:19:34.570
Let's be friends.

00:19:39.120 --> 00:19:41.000
Carrots. Carrots.

00:19:41.000 --> 00:19:45.590
Carrots. Carrots. Carrots. Carrots. Carrots...

00:19:45.850 --> 00:19:48.840
No, I shall never be friends with you!

00:19:49.860 --> 00:19:54.010
And I don't want to be, Gilbert Blythe!

00:19:55.210 --> 00:19:57.030
All right, Anne Shirley!

00:19:57.350 --> 00:19:59.890
I'll never ask you to be friends again.

00:20:00.140 --> 00:20:01.510
And I don't care either!

00:20:29.620 --> 00:20:31.510
Anne! It's Anne!

00:20:32.180 --> 00:20:33.750
Anne! Anne's here!

00:20:33.750 --> 00:20:35.040
It's really her!

00:20:35.040 --> 00:20:36.910
Anne! You're Anne, aren't you?

00:20:37.340 --> 00:20:39.400
Yes. It's me.

00:20:39.970 --> 00:20:42.260
Oh, Anne Shirley!

00:20:42.400 --> 00:20:44.290
Are you really Anne?

00:20:46.540 --> 00:20:48.670
You're really alive, Anne Shirley!

00:20:50.310 --> 00:20:51.910
Thank Goodness!

00:20:51.910 --> 00:20:53.800
Where were you, Anne?

00:20:54.240 --> 00:20:58.860
When the boat sank
I climbed up on one of the piles.

00:20:59.200 --> 00:21:01.970
I saw you running from afar.

00:21:02.050 --> 00:21:04.960
We went to Diana's house to find help.

00:21:04.960 --> 00:21:08.250
But there was no one home.
And then... And then...

00:21:09.350 --> 00:21:12.600
We thought you were drowned

00:21:12.600 --> 00:21:15.850
and... and we didn't know what to do.

00:21:21.540 --> 00:21:24.170
But Anne, how did you escape?

00:21:25.910 --> 00:21:29.620
Gilbert Blythe came along in a
boat and brought me to land.

00:21:29.620 --> 00:21:32.840
Oh! Gilbert saved you?

00:21:32.850 --> 00:21:36.480
How splendid of him!
Why, it's so romantic!

00:21:36.480 --> 00:21:39.800
Of course you'll speak to him after this.

00:21:39.870 --> 00:21:42.310
Of course I won't! Never!

00:21:43.070 --> 00:21:49.190
And Jane Andrews... I don't want ever
to hear the word 'romantic' again!

00:21:58.050 --> 00:22:03.510
This matter of Elaine
shocked all parents in Avonlea.

00:22:03.860 --> 00:22:07.590
Especially the parents
of the children of the Story Club.

00:22:07.590 --> 00:22:13.300
They never allowed their
children to play by the river again.

00:22:13.960 --> 00:22:21.670
A good cry had soothed Anne's nerves
and restored her to her wonted cheerfulness.

00:22:21.670 --> 00:22:26.050
Anne, will you ever have any sense?

00:22:26.340 --> 00:22:28.090
Oh, don't worry.

00:22:28.350 --> 00:22:33.600
I think my prospects of becoming
sensible are brighter now than ever.

00:22:34.000 --> 00:22:35.780
I don't see how.

00:22:36.210 --> 00:22:39.190
Ever since I came to Green
Gables I've been making mistakes,

00:22:39.800 --> 00:22:44.290
and each mistake has helped
to cure me of some great shortcoming.

00:22:45.300 --> 00:22:49.690
Today's mistake is going
to cure me of one shortcoming too.

00:22:50.430 --> 00:22:52.040
And what would that be?

00:22:52.210 --> 00:22:54.650
Is going to cure me of being too romantic.

00:22:55.280 --> 00:22:56.710
It is no use trying to be

00:22:56.710 --> 00:23:00.570
romantic in Avonlea, unlike in the
towered Camelot hundreds of years ago.

00:23:01.800 --> 00:23:05.720
But romance is not appreciated now.

00:23:07.220 --> 00:23:09.570
I feel quite sure that you will soon see

00:23:09.570 --> 00:23:11.880
a great improvement
in me in this respect, Marilla.

00:23:11.890 --> 00:23:13.740
I'm sure I hope so.

00:23:14.080 --> 00:23:17.330
I do not wish to shorten my lifespan.

00:23:29.800 --> 00:23:30.920
Anne...

00:23:32.680 --> 00:23:37.280
Don't give up all your romance, Anne.

00:23:38.320 --> 00:23:39.410
Matthew!

00:23:40.490 --> 00:23:45.170
Well... a little of it is a good thing.

00:23:45.500 --> 00:23:50.930
Not too much, of course...
But keep a little of it, Anne.

00:23:51.280 --> 00:23:52.780
Keep a little of it.

00:23:52.890 --> 00:23:54.150
Thank you, Matthew.

00:23:54.770 --> 00:23:57.450
I won't ever forget what you said.

00:24:17.800 --> 00:24:24.070
One day, Diana brought
some news about an invitation.

00:24:24.720 --> 00:24:27.600
Next episode of Anne of Green Gables:

00:24:27.870 --> 00:24:29.590
An Epoch in Anne's Life

00:24:29.650 --> 00:24:30.600
Please watch!
